ul.li:
delegation_chain claim: An explicit,
cryptographically signed delegation record of all delegation hops,
which identity chaining does not define;

It MUST be less than or equal to the access token's
iat (issued at) claim, since the delegation event
occurs before or at the time the token is issued;

delegation_proposal (OPTIONAL): The
delegator-signed prospective record, when delegator
non-repudiation is used (see above);

Verify as_signature on each delegation record using the
signing key of the AS identified by the record's
as_id field (which may differ across records);

AS Signature (SHOULD when present):
Confirms the delegation was authorized by the AS and the
record has not been tampered with;

For the initial delegation hop, the AS enforces a
freshness window on the subject_token's
iat claim (RECOMMENDED skew: 5 minutes);

Short token lifetimes (RECOMMENDED:
5 to 15 minutes) limit the window during which a stolen
or replayed token remains valid;

Sender-constrained tokens (DPoP or
mTLS) ensure that a stolen token cannot be used by a
different party;

Token introspection
() enables real-time revocation
status checking;

ol.li:
Verify prev_record_hash linkage on multi-record
            chains: record[i].prev_record_hash equals the
            SHA-256 hash of the canonical serialization (per
            ) of record[i+1] (MUST;
            reject with invalid_delegation_chain if missing
            or mismatched)
